{{Quote|A pauldron would be in order.|[[The Armorer]], to [[Din Djarin]]|<ref name="Chapter 1" />}}
'''Pauldrons''' were a type of [[armor]] worn by [[soldier]]s of the [[Galactic Republic]],<ref name="TCW" /> the [[Galactic Empire]],<ref name="ANH" /> the [[First Order]],<ref name="TFA" /> and [[Mandalore]]. These represented the wearer's [[Military rank|rank]] or affiliation. These varied in [[color]],<ref name="Ultimate" /> and could sometimes feature symbols associated with the wearer's [[commander]].<ref name="TIE">{{Rebels|Through Imperial Eyes}}</ref>

==Galactic Republic==
[[File:TCW_Tano_unit_2.png|thumb|left|300px|Clone Captain [[Rex]] wears a pauldron]]
The [[Galactic Republic]]'s specialized and officer [[clone trooper]]s utilized pauldrons. [[Advanced Recon Commando]]s were known to utilize them, as well as [[Clone Sergeant]]s, [[Clone Lieutenant]]s, [[Clone Captain]]s,<ref name="ARC Troopers">{{TCW|ARC Troopers (episode)}}</ref> and [[Clone Commander]]s.<ref name="Point Rain">{{TCW|Landing at Point Rain}}</ref>

The [[Wookiee warrior]]s of the Republic [[planet]] [[Kashyyyk]] utilized decorative pauldrons.<ref name="CVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref>

==Galactic Empire==
[[File:Shadow_trooper_pauldron.png|thumb|right|250px|An Imperial shadow trooper equipped with a type of pauldron.]]
Members of the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Stormtrooper Corps]] known as [[Stormtrooper Commander]]s wore pauldrons to represent their position as [[officer]]s.<ref name="JFO">''[[Star Wars Jedi: Fallen Order]]''</ref> Pauldrons also were placed on the armor of [[Desert stormtrooper|sandtroopers]],<ref name="ANH" /> [[magma trooper]]s,<ref name="Battlefront">''[[Star Wars Battlefront]]''</ref> [[Purge Trooper]]s,<ref name="Part IV">{{Kenobi|Part IV}}</ref> and [[death trooper]]s.<ref name="Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> A black colored pauldron seen on a stormtrooper indicated an enlisted trooper<ref name="Ultimate" /> but also could be used for some Stormtrooper Commanders,<ref name="Crawler Commandeers">{{Rebels|Crawler Commandeers}}</ref> such as [[corporal]]s<ref name="Princess">{{Rebels|A Princess on Lothal}}</ref> and [[sergeant]]s.<ref name="Databank Sergeant">{{AtomicMassGames|url=transmission/databank-download-stormtrooper-sergeant-stormtroopers-preview-article|text=Databank Download: Stormtrooper Sergeant & Stormtroopers Preview Article}}</ref> Indeed, in the case of Stormtrooper Commanders, pauldron color could indicate the wearer's [[Military rank|rank]], position or specialization.<ref name="ANH" /> White was for sergeants,<ref name="Ultimate" /> red was for squad leaders,<ref name="Gathering Forces">{{Rebels|Gathering Forces}}</ref> and orange was for unit leaders,<ref name="Ultimate" /> including a squad leader,<ref name="ANH" /> sergeants,<ref name="AMG Stormtrooper">{{Twitter|atomicmassgames|status/1743316493343826118|[[Atomic Mass Games]]|quote=A Stormtrooper Sergeant serves as Secondary support for Darth Vader in the Fear & Dead Men Squad Pack for STAR WARS: Shatterpoint.|archiveurl=https://archive.is/snQUQ}}</ref> [[captain]]s,<ref name="ANH paperback">[[Star Wars: A New Hope (paperback novel)|''Star Wars: A New Hope'' junior novelization]]</ref><ref name="ANH" /> or commanders.<ref name="Dark Temple 1">[[Jedi Fallen Order - Dark Temple 1|''Jedi Fallen Order - Dark Temple'' 1]]</ref>

[[Incinerator stormtrooper|Incinerator troopers]] wore red while [[artillery stormtrooper]]s wore yellow.<ref name="Recon Missions">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Recon Missions]]''</ref><ref name="Strike Missions">{{SW|url=games-apps/disneyxd-star-wars-rebels-strike-missions|text=''Star Wars Rebels: Strike Missions''|int=Star Wars Rebels: Strike Missions|nolive=1}}</ref> Imperial stormtroopers stationed aboard [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn's]] [[flagship]] ''[[Chimaera]]'' wore pauldrons that, although in the normal color variations, featured a symbol of a stylized [[Chimaera (creature)|chimaera]] in the middle. This symbol was associated with the Grand [[Admiral]], and also appeared on the [[Imperial military uniforms|uniforms]] of [[Imperial officer]]s aboard the [[Starship|ship]].<ref name="TIE" /> Death troopers used black pauldrons to signify specialists, who had access to additional weapons and equipment. The pauldrons provided additional information when viewed through a [[Death trooper armor|death trooper's helmet]].<ref name="Visual Guide" />

==First Order==
The rise of the [[First Order]] witnessed the continuity of Imperial customs, one such tradition being the use of pauldrons to denote rank or specialty, such as [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] officers in the [[First Order military]]. Officers wore red pauldrons, sergeants wore black, and squad leaders wore white.<ref name="TFA" />

